<title>USA: Treasury's Rubin reiterates U.S. favors strong dlr.</title>
<headline>Treasury's Rubin reiterates U.S. favors strong dlr.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin on Monday reiterated the U.S. favors a strong dollar.</p>
<p>&quot;We favor a strong dollar, as we always have and for the reasons we always have. It helps keep inflation down, it helps keep interest rates down, both of which is good for the economy,&quot; said Rubin at a briefing.</p>
</text>
